olarships Campus Ministries Volunteering Living Housing and Dining Services ID Center Health and Counseling Services Transportation Campus Police & Safety Technology Community CommuniTEAMS CODE 4 STEM Academy CODE for Commonwealth & Country Community and Economic Impact Military Friendly Campus REACHland Connect Campus and Community Facilities Student Success Pitt-Johnstown Book Center Owen Library Real World Readiness Student Conduct & Judicial Affairs Winterfest 2025 Homecoming Homecoming Court Athletics Zamias Aquatic Center Wellness Center Alumni Alumni Association Board of Directors Application Packet Alumni Events Alumni Golf Classic Mountain Cat Tournament Pitt-Johnstown Success Stories Homecoming Alumni First: Pitt-Johnstown Business Directory Giving to Pitt-Johnstown Giving to Pitt-Johnstown A Message from the President Your Gift Matters Donor-Supported Funds Overview Undergraduate Research Faculty-Student Mentorship Projects Faculty-Student Mentorship Projects Here are the recent research, scholarship, and creative activities supported by the President’s Mentorship Fund for Faculty-Student Scholarship for the 2025 - 2026 academic year. Spring 2026 Recipients Dr. Cynthia Ofori-Boateng and students Cameron Skodny, Singh Gurjeet, Morgan Hill, Lucas Errett, Kaylee Harshman, Gavin Cleary, Maxwell Cunliffe: Biorefining of Waste Materials into Biodiesel, Bioethanol and Biogas – Exergy Efficiency Assessment Drs. Geeta Verma and Ramesh Singh and students Theodore Markow, Nicholas Renzulli, Kaycie Cleric: Molecular Tuning of Lanthanide Binding Tag (LBT) Peptide for Selective Separation of Rare Earth Elements (Extension) Dr. Manisha Nigam and student Katrina Diaz: Supporting Student Scholarship and Professional Development for the 2026 American Chemical Society National Meeting Dr. Stephanie Jimenez and students Hoda Barakat and Kelly Hutchinson: Travel to the 2026 Annual Meeting of the Eastern Psychological Association Dr. Ryan Kerrigan and student Ian Gasior: Benefit from Burden: Significance of Coal Refuse as a Rare Earth Elements Resource Dr. Jill Henning and student Nicholos-Octavius Harrell: Biological Evaluation of Novel Amide-Containing Quorum Sensing Inhibitors Dr. Ryan Kerrigan and student Jessica Hollan: U-Pb Zircon Geochronology of Pegmatites in Chester County, Pennsylvania: Insights into Appalachian Tectonic Evolution Dr. Bruce Robart and student Benjamin Milkie: Biogeography, Taxonomic and Genetic Relationships Among the Pedicularis sudetica Plant Species Complex Drs. Sharon Bertsch and Steven Stern and students Sadie Swank and Maggie Verostick: Travel to the 2026 Annual Meeting of the Eastern Psychological Association Fall 2025 Recipients Dr. Marsha Grimminger and student Tracy Yu: Spray deposition of titanium films for use in Dye Sensitized Solar Cells Drs. Geeta Verma and Ramesh Singh and students Theodore Markow, Nicholas Renzulli, Kaycie Cleric: Molecular Tuning of Lanthanide Binding Tag (LPT) Peptide for Selective Separation of Rare Earth Elements Dr. Laura Ritchey and students Evan Lenz, Samuel Allshouse, Ian Yatchik: Using RT-qPCR to evaluate the degree of hidden breaks in the growth of rice cprRNA Dr. Manisha Nigam and students Nathan Fisanick and Katrina Diaz: Development of Environmentally-Benign Reactions for the Organic Curriculum Dr. Ryan Kerrigan and student Jessica Hollan: Tracing Tectonic Origins: Geochemistry of Pennsylvania Pegmatites Dr. Natalie Conrad Barnyak and students Isabella Dadura, Emily Oliver, Madison Putman: The Kaleidoscope Classroom with Infinite Possibilities: Celebrating Multiculturalism Within Early Childhood Settings Through Diversity Stations Dr. Bethany McConnell and students Austin Deweese, Juliana Rosetti, Shallyn Shank, Luke Rozich: Student Teachers Measuring Personal Progress Goals for Classroom Management Dr. Stephan Ohl and students Megan Edder, Brandon Everhart, Everett Walker: Authentic Facial Expression and Body Language Animations for Virtual Student Characters Dr. Jill Henning and students Abigail Berry and Atlas Brogaard: Knowledge, Attitudes, and Practices Surrounding Tick-Borne Disease Prevention in Southwestern Pennsylvania Previous Recipients Spring 2025 Dr. Cynthia Ofori-Boateng and students Lopez Marcos, Verbus Jillian, Yu Tracy, Ethan Craft, Olivia Giardina, Gurjeet Singh, Cameron Skodny, and Kush Srivastava: Optimization of Anaerobic Co-digestion of Food Waste and Spent Coffee Grounds for Biogas Generation Dr. Sharon Bertsch and student Maggie Verostick: Travel to the 2025 Annual Meeting of the Eastern Psychological Association Dr. Elaine Wilson and students Courtney Hilyer and Morgan Homer: Empowering Inclusion: Educators’ Knowledge, Perceptions, & Implementation on Assistive Technology in the Rural Classroom Dr. Elaine Wilson and students Eryn Marsh and Emily Karl: Building Bridge(s): Empowering Transitions Through Collaborative Teaching Dr. Manisha Nigam and student Katrina Diaz: Exploration of a green reduction in multi-step synthesis Dr. Christopher Cogenhour and students Luka Hodgson and Jenna Tallman: Linking watershed process to hillslope stability in an incised Appalachian Plateau stream: Rocky Run on the Pitt-Johnstown campus Dr. James Bilitsky and student Riley Figard: Hear & Sing VR: Interactive Pitch Training for Kids with Profound Hearing Loss Dr. Ladan Momayez and student Noah Massart: Numerical Analysis of Angle of Attack Influence on Momentum Thickness Boundary Layer Fall 2024 Dr. Sharon Bertsch and students Colton Nesmith and Nicole Sukenik: The Limitations of Testing Accommodations for Students with ADHD Dr. Ryan Kerrigan and student Isabelle Boyer: From Waste to Wealth: Analyzing Rare Earth Elements in Coal Refuse Piles Dr. Ryan Kerrigan and student Christopher Howard: U-Pb isotopic dating of the volcanic ash layers in New Paris, PA to provide insight into regional depositional and tectonic activity Dr. Manisha Nigam and students Karin Ilagin and Katrina Diaz: Microwave-Assisted Multi-Step Synthesis Dr. Bethany McConnell and students Courtney Hilyer, Emily Karl, and Morgan Homer: Our Experiences of Getting Professional Development through CEC Mentorship While Student Teaching Dr. Bethany McConnell and student Eryn March: Using Social Media as an Innovative Way for College Faculty to Recruit Future Teachers Ms. Geeta Verma: Improving Resources for Hands-on Beer Brewing and Winemaking Learning Experience for Engineering Students Spring 2024 Dr. Laura Ritchey and students Evan Lenz and Maxwell Cunliffe : Using RT-qPCR to evaluate the degree of hidden breaks in rice cprRN Dr. Bruce Robart and students Selena Laughlin and Zachary Connor : Employing Gene Coalescence to Evaluate Past Refugia and Dispersal Hypotheses for Pedicularis racemosa, Part II Dr. Manisha Nigam and student Karin Ilagin : Michael Addition Reaction in a Green Solvent Dr. Cynthia Ofori-Boateng and students Desean Hunter, Abigail Knapp, Marcos Lopez, Flash Stroop, Jillian Verbus, Tracy Yu : Sustainability Analysis of Waste Oil and Spent Coffee Grounds Biodiesel Production Technologies Dr. Elaine Wilson and students Emily Elson and Hannah Ribblett : BRIDGE to Independence for Students in Special Education Dr. Stephanie Jimenez and student Juliana Butz : Travel to the 2024 Annual Meeting of the Eastern Psychological Association, Feb. 29 - March 2 Fall 2023 Dr. Ryan Bird and students Roman Beran and Joe Holecz: Dynamics of Peptide Bonds, Part II: The Study of Acetohydroxamic Acid using Chirped-Pulsed FTMW Spectroscopy Dr. Bruce Robart and students Anna Startari and Zachary Connor: Employing Gene Coalescence to Evaluate Past Refugia and Dispersal Hypotheses for Pedicularis racemose Mr. John Teacher and students Saara Alsayed, Jay Miller, Gloria Mancilla, and Amity Shallenberger: Designing with and creating projected image and videography while merging technologies Dr. Ryan Kerrigan and student Aleya Schreckengost: Examining Minera Fluid Inclusions to Assess the Economic Potential of Allegheny Hydrothermal Systems Dr. Manisha Nigam and student Korina Pebley: Green Reduction in Organic Synthetic Sequence Dr. Mitzi Schaney and student Nicholas Scelsi: Trace Metal Analysis of Soils in Prince Gallitzin State Park Ms. Geeta Verma and students Aidan McMoil, Abigail Knapp, Flash Stroop and Nicole Hudak: Hands-On Beer Brewing Experience in Chemical Engineering Senior Project Spring 2023 Dr. Sharon Bertsch and students Isabella Nagy & Anthony McCann: Influence of Ethnic Background on Perceptions of Sexism and Infidelity Dr. Luis Bonachea and students Katherine Pugar, Claire Hummel, and Alexis Lupey: Creating a Digital Teaching Collection of Spider Identification, Taxonomy, and Reproductive Anatomy Dr. Ryan Kerrigan and student Christopher Howard: Examination of the 417-million-year-old Volcanic Ash Layers in New Paris, PA to Understand the Building of the Appalachians Dr. John Mullennix and students Leah Miller and Rachel Strode: Information about Artist Drug Use Affects Viewers’ Impressions of Art Dr. Manisha Nigam and Dr. Matthew Tracey and students Elaynah Pirzada & Michael Moslak: Development of a Multi-Step Green Organic Synthetic Sequence Fall 2022 Dr. Bruce Robart with students Anna Staratari and Briana Maxwell: Taxonomic and Genetic Relationships Among Members of the Pedicularis sudetica Complex, part 2 Dr. Ramesh Singh and students Abigail Knapp, Renee Firek, Megan Gray, Aidan McMoil, Nicholas Bliss, Ian Dundas, Nicholas Gorschak, Devin Gomish and Katherine Croyle: A tmospheric Carbon Dioxide Fixation by Chlorella vulgaris Microalgae Cultivated in a Photobioreactor and Electroflocculation of Chlorella vulgaris using Electrodes of Different Materials Dr. Susan Wieczorek and students Angel Auxtero & Hannah Larson: It Always Gets Better:  It’s Life; It Has To” (Addiction and Survival) and Illness is a Tunnel; Not a Cave (COVID-19 Experience) Undergraduate Research Fall Into Research SPACE Faculty-Student Mentorship Projects Grants Services Academics in the News UPJ