    "https://www.hr.pitt.edu/current-employees/employee-labor-relations/workplace-postings": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Required Workplace Postings | Human Resources Skip to main content Office of Human Resources Search Open Navigation pitt_25_custom Benefits Health & Welfare Education Time Off Leave Types Retirement Savings Work-Life Balance Benefits Notices Benefits FAQs Open Enrollment Compensation Staff Compensation Structure Fair Labor Standards Act Compensation Resources Compensation FAQs Employee & Labor Relations Clearances & Training Collective Bargaining Agreements Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Required Workplace Postings Staff Handbook Employee & Labor Relations FAQ Form I-9 Employment Verification Learning & Development Faculty & Staff Development Program Online Learning with LinkedIn Learning Organization Development Learning & Development FAQs Supervisor Essentials Hiring Contact OHR Careers at Pitt New Hire Onboarding Breadcrumb Employee & Labor Relations Required Workplace Postings The following documents are required to be posted in common area/s of the workplace: Abstract of Equal Pay Law (PDF) Drug-Free Schools Annual Notification (PDF) Education Provisions of the Pennsylvania Human Relations Act (PDF) Employee Polygraph Protection Act Notice (EPPA )(PDF) Employee Rights and Responsibilities Under the Family Medical Leave Act (FMLA) (PDF) Employee Rights Under the Fair Labor Standards Act (PDF) Employment Provisions of the Pennsylvania Human Relations Act (PDF) Executive Order 14026 - Minimum Wage If You Have the Right to Work (PDF) Job Safety and Health: It's the Law (Occupational Safety and Health Act/OSHA) (PDF) Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal (PDF) Notice of Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy Statement Pennsylvania Labor Relations Board - Graduate Student Unit Clarification Petition (PDF) Pennsylvania Labor Relations Board - Standardized Patient Unit Clarification Petition (PDF) Pennsylvania Minimum Wage Law (PDF) Pennsylvania Right to Know Act (PDF) Pittsburgh Fair Employment Practice Notice (PDF) Security and Fire Safety Report Summary of Work-Related Injuries and Illnesses - All Campuses (OSHA's Form 300A) (PDF) Unemployment Compensation (PDF) University Pay Transparency Statement (PDF) Veteran Benefits and Services (PDF) We Participate in E-Verify (PDF) Whistleblower Laws Workers' Compensation (Pennsylvania) Your Rights Under USERRA (PDF) H-1B Notices​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​ All H-1B notices posted after Feb. 1, 2024, can be found on the Office of International Services website. Outside Pennsylvania/Out-of-State Employees Expand the drop-down menu to find a list of Workers' Compensation-related workplace postings (PDFs) for out-of-state employees. For accessibility questions related to these workplace postings, please submit an inquiry to the Office of Human Resources. Workers' Compensation Postings for Out-of-State Employees Alabama Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Florida Georgia Illinois Indiana Kentucky Maryland Massachusetts Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Nebraska New Hampshire New Jersey New York North Carolina Oklahoma Rhode Island South Carolina Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Washington, D.C. West Virginia Wisconsin Employee & Labor Relations Clearances & Training Collective Bargaining Agreements Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Required Workplace Postings Staff Handbook Employee & Labor Relations FAQ Form I-9 Employment Verification Employee & Labor Relations Inquiries Employee & Labor Relations Phone: 412-624-7000 Fax: 412-624-8063 Submit a Question or Comment to Employee & Labor Relations Find your assigned ERLR Representative (via Pitt Passport) University Policies & Procedures Visit this page for a list of the policies and procedures of the University. Find a Policy or Procedure Office of Human Resources Main Navigation Benefits Compensation Employee & Labor Relations Learning & Development Hiring Contact OHR Careers at Pitt New Hire Onboarding About Our Office About OHR OHR Directory OHR Organizational Chart Recognizing Employee Excellence Required Workplace Postings For Supervisors Supervisor Essentials (SharePoint) Hiring New Talent Onboard New Employees Resources for Managers (SharePoint) Employment Verification 200 South Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer/disability/veteran. Accessibility Statement Close Navigation Benefits Compensation Employee & Labor Relations Learning & Development Hiring Contact OHR Careers at Pitt New Hire Onboarding About Our Office OHR Organizational Chart Recognizing Employee Excellence Required Workplace Postings About OHR OHR Directory 200 South Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Close Search Human Resources Search"
    },
    "https://www.risk.pitt.edu/workers-compensation/designated-wc-provider-panels-and-workplace-postings": {
      "title": "Designated Workers’ Compensation (WC) Health Care Provider Panels and Workplace Postings",
      "description": "Designated Workers’ Compensation (WC) Health Care Provider Panels and Workplace Postings | Risk Management | University of Pittsburgh Skip to main content Office of Risk Management F&O Find People Use this for to search the site. Search Toggle navigation Home Accident Reporting Automobile Accident/Incident Reporting University-Owned Property Insurance Auto Financial Responsibility Insurance ID Card Certificate of Insurance Property Minimum Insurance Requirements for Contracts Med Mal/Credentialing Medical Malpractice Insurance Policy Information Medical Malpractice and Credentialing FAQ's Work-Related Injuries Reporting a Work-Related Injury Designated Workers’ Compensation (WC) Health Care Provider Panels and Workplace Postings Supervisor Responsibilities Frequently Asked Questions for Employees Living/Working in PA Forms Addition/Deletion Form: Fine Art and Historical Treasure Collections Addition/Deletion Form: Leased Space/Contents Costs Only University-Owned/Property, Buildings & Contents Staff Designated Workers’ Compensation (WC) Health Care Provider Panels and Workplace Postings WC Health Care Provider Panels All panels have been revised as of 7/1/2026 unless otherwise indicated.  Please replace the current posting of panels in your common areas with the updated version. (Check this website regularly for any updates). Oakland Bradford Greensburg Johnstown Mechanicsburg Titusville Pymatuning Remember to periodically check this website for the most updated listings. Workplace Postings Pennsylvania: The following documents are to be posted in common areas of the workplace: Remember: It Is Important To Tell Your Employer About Your Injury Form (PDF) Employee Acknowledgment of Rights & Duties Form (PDF) Designated Workers’ Compensation (WC) Health Care Provider Panels - select your campus (PDF) Outside of Pennsylvania: Contact HR/Employee Relations to request the appropriate required workplace posting for the state where you or your employee will live and work. Work-Related Injuries Reporting a Work-Related Injury Designated Workers’ Compensation (WC) Health Care Provider Panels and Workplace Postings Supervisor Responsibilities Frequently Asked Questions for Employees Living/Working in PA Office of Risk Management University of Pittsburgh 3017 Cathedral of Learning Pittsburgh, PA 15260 Hours: 8:30 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. M-F Divisions Controller's Office Financial Operations Investment Office Office of the Treasurer Revised 08/21/26 Copyright 2026"
    },
